{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1558387-metamagic-bonuses","id":1558387,"title":"Metamagic Bonuses","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-02-19T13:27:54-08:00","id":1558387,"title":"Metamagic Bonuses","content":"There are some abilities that come from having a Sphere at a certain rank that are not themselves spells, just preturnatural or supernatural abilities the mage now always has.<br /> <br /> The clearest examples are from Prime At Prime 1 a mage can store more Quintessence than his Avatar rating. No spell is needed.<br /> <br /> In previous editions a mage with at least Prime 1 could sense the casting of magic even without active Prime senses.<br /> <br /> In the optional Anti-Magic rule, a mage can roll Prime (not Arete) to stop opposing magic. <br /> <br /> Then there's the way range extension works. Range extension is Correspondence 2, but a mage can't extend spells of Rank X without at least Correspondence X. So Correspondence 3 unlocks range extension for Rank 3 max spells, Correspondence 4 unlocks it for Rank 4 max spells, etc. The mage isn't using higher ranks of Correspondence, but he has to have them. A kind of gatekeeping form of metamagic.<br /> <br /> Astral Immersion in the Digital Web requires Correspondence 2, but is not a magical effect.<br /> <br /> A mage with Spirit can use Countermagic to soak a spirit's rage based damage and certain other attacks from spirits.<br /> <br /> Mages with Entropy 4 are immune to Calcify.<br /> <br /> Time 2 cancels out the Multiple Opponents Penalty if the mage has an active Correspondence, Mind, or Time sensory effect going.<br /> <br /> A mage who has Mind 1 or Correspondence 1 and has an active sensory effect from any sphere can read an opponent from a distance.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, there's the crossover friendly house rule that mages can soak Agg damage with the Life Sphere.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Obviously some of these are quite situational and maybe not all that important.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> My three questions are:<br /> <br /> 1) Are there any that already exist (in any edition) that I am missing?<br /> <br /> 2) Are there any that you think should exist? Or spell abilities that make more sense as metamagic effects?<br /> <br /> 3) If we hypothetically wanted to pad out every sphere and rank with one or more metamagic abilities, what would be some good suggestions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-19T13:38:15-08:00","id":1558388,"title":"","content":"Look at Attainments in <b>Mage: the Awakening 2e</b>. They're basically this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-20T05:12:38-08:00","id":1558393,"title":"","content":"All spheres unlock basic Countermagick for their effects. A Mage with Prime 1 can use Offensive Countermagick that on top of having the cahnce to alter the target of spells, it's the only way of targeting spells that aren't targeted at yourself with countermagick. Prime 2 can use Anti-Magick, that allows to roll Prime (rather than Arete) to increase spell difficulties.<br /> <br /> None of these are ordinary rotes, while Anti-Magick takes the cake of being odd rolling Prime rather than Arete, there's no reason why, say, Forces 1 could snuf out a fireball. Nor why Prime 1 would be needed to afect a fireball not being casted at yourself. Rather it's sort of prerequisite to extend a general &quot;resist magick&quot; thing that mages just seem to have <hr /><br /> Some of the Archspheres on MotA seem to be more akin to metamagic abilities than Spheres - and there's one in particular that seems to actually be inspired in a sort of hidden rule, and could be easily added to at least some Spheres at level 5 as a passive: Forces 6 x2 to successes.<br /> <br /> There's a sort of hidden rule about rotes that use Forces 5/Prime 5 to cause damage that make the damage 4 x successes instead of 2 x successes. You can see that on multiple rotes. It sort of cancels out (roughly) the fact that using Spheres at a higger level has an increased difficulty (and thus would cause less damage than a lower level effect). So I think it's not a bad thing to have as basis to solve a problem.<br /> <br /> It could be worded as &quot;Effects that include x Sphere at level 5 count double the final number of successes for the purposes of causing damage&quot;.<br /> <br /> Extending that to everything rather than just damage can be a bit overpowered, tho. But, then, lvl 5 Spheres are supposed to feel godlike so maybe that's not a terrible thing either. <hr /><br /> I think it could be cool if Life 1 allowed to do the &quot;body control&quot; things (the optional rule in Abilities) w/o needing Esoterica. After all such mages are much more in tune with their own bodies and bodily functions than even experts on the field of body control.<br /> <br /> Similarly other sphere levels could either provide or mimick the use of abilities related to the subject of the Sphere w/o needing to cast anything.<br /> <br /> Spirit 2 can be used to communicate with spirits w/o using abilities. The way it's worded seems like it's an Effect. But that could easily be a passive ability instead, rather than having to cast a spell, calculate duration, calculate penalties for juggling multiple effects if applicable, etc ... just to talk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-20-2026, 08:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-23T08:17:46-08:00","id":1558470,"title":"","content":"I can add two more possibilities.<br /> <br /> The first is that the Temporal Immunity abilities of Time 5 would make a lot of sense as metamagic abilities. At the very least, it would make sense if Time Masters are automatically immune to being erased if the timeline shifts.<br /> <br /> Also, if Permanent Effects (as opposed to unending spells) are meant to be a Rank 5 ability for most spheres, it would also make sense if mages only had to have the sphere at Rank 5, not use it. That is, a Life Master could permanently change a fish to a frog permanently using Life 3, while an Adept could only cast a spell with a permanent duration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-20T22:11:39-07:00","id":1561987,"title":"","content":"I think the whole list should first be revised. Remove some effects, refine others. Then start to add those passive abilities.<br /> <br /> And yes, Mage the Awakening is overall a good source of ideas, not only through Attainments. Mage Sight is another example that make some sense. Masters of the Art is also a good source of ideas, which makes for one of the few uses it's good at.<br /> <br /> Prime 1: how important it is? How much the game understates the value of Tass integrated on Instruments? How much it oversells Quintessence or underuse it?<br /> <br /> IME some players fall in the trap of buying Prime and never actually using it because they have no use for Quintessence.<br /> <br /> Sensing at 1: I think this should be universal. If you have a Sphere at all, you can attune to that aspect of reality without having to stop to cast something all the time. Would even help STs as it opens a new avenue to deliver plot hooks.<br /> <br /> Rolling Prime for antimagic helps how, again? I'm always confused on why do that if Arete is already at least at the same value.<br /> <br /> The Correspondence requisite is positively bad. I understand why it's there, but I don't think this is the solution. Now could be a good moment to add Quintessence costs, instead.<br /> <br /> Gatekeeping the Digital Web behind Corr 2 is a weirdly specific requisite. I mean, got the idea, but this is not the only space in the Umbra that translates relationship vectors into space.<br /> <br /> I'm ok with Spirit soaking Spiritual damage and I don't remember what's Calcify.<br /> <br /> Time 2 cancels out the Multiple Opponents Penalty is unnecessary, Mind 1 or Correspondence 1 read an opponent from a distance is unnecessary, soak Agg with Life by default is weird.<br /> <br /> Agree with the ideas for Rank 5 Spheres, the access to Permanent effects and certain immunities could be abilities rather than effects.<br /> <br /> So, I think each Sphere should have at least a level 1 perception ability and a level 5 immunity and Permanent spells. Maybe other sphere levels could apply similarly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-21T09:51:50-07:00","id":1562000,"title":"","content":"Hmm... Problem is that, yes, while this can be inferred from the text, it is not explicit. For example, the extended range effects using Corr doesn't automatically translate to &quot;Get Corr and automatically get the ability to cast at a distance&quot;. It's more that you have to cast a conjunctional effect adding Corr to it - it becomes a &quot;new spell&quot; that can be cast at a distance, rather than a natural ability added to your spells.<br /> <br /> For the Prime 1 effects, I also don't remember them being automatic either. &quot;You can sense magic with Prime 1&quot; has never been stated to be AUTOMATIC - in fact, for what I myself have always understood, you'd have to cast a Prime 1 effects, and then voil\u00e1, sense magic. Therefore, &quot;Sense Magic&quot; is a Prime 1 &quot;spell&quot; - there is, you have to actively cast it in order to use it.<br /> <br /> Likewise, the only thing I remember about storing Quint beyond Avatar lvl was &quot;you can do it with Prime 1&quot;. For my understanding, that has always meant that it involves &quot;Cast the spell: Quint Absorb&quot;. <br /> <br /> I mean, I'm not against having some things becoming &quot;natural abilities&quot; once you unlock them, I like the idea, I'm just saying that I never understood this to be the case","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29126-phooku","name":"Phooku","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-21T13:42:45-07:00","id":1562008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phooku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1558387-metamagic-bonuses?p=1562000#post1562000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, I'm not against having some things becoming &quot;natural abilities&quot; once you unlock them, I like the idea, I'm just saying that I never understood this to be the case</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;ability&quot; isn't having access to extended ranges, it's to be able to apply Corr to a given Effect.<br /> <br /> By the rules, if you have Correspondence 3 and Forces 4, you can't use any of your Corr effects with 4th level Forces Effects. For effects that require Forces 4, your effective Corr level is 0.<br /> <br /> Prime 1 used to let you sense Magic passively on previous editions. It's not in Revised or M20, but was in 1st and, IIRC, 2nd.<br /> <br /> Storing more Quintessence is also clearly not an Effect. Prime 1 doesn't say you can make an Effect to gather Quintessence or to store more Quintessence, it says you can store more, period.<br /> <br /> Were that the case, it would have been worded very differently, and would contradict higher levels when gathering/absorbing Quintessence becomes in fact accessible. It would also mean your extra Quint is temporary, since the effect would have a duration after which you go back to Avatar Rating, and the excess would bleed away.<br /> <br /> First is clear on the rules, second is old and only brought up for discussion, third I never met anyone who read that as an effect rather than a passive change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}